All,

In the case of a lateral connection with a PE Ball Valve, electrofusion fit=
tings are typically used.  In the interest of minimizing risk the following=
 guidance applies.

If socket electrofusing to pipe, the pipe must be scraped per standard prac=
tice.

If the socket electrofusion is to a plain end that is part of a molded fitt=
ing (such as a BF Fitting, EF Branch Saddle, or PE Ball Valve) it is not ne=
cessary and good risk management practice not to scrape that end in order t=
o insure the best possible interface between the plain end and the socket. =
 All other preparations are the same for both cases.

The reason it is necessary to scrape pipe is because the surface is likely =
to have been oxidized by UV exposure from sunlight and contaminated by dirt=
 and so on from handling and laying around exposed.  These effects make a p=
roper fusion unachievable.

The reason it is not necessary to scrape molded fittings is because these w=
ill have been packaged and protected from contaminants and UV degradation (=
assuming that is the case of course).  This is not saying it is wrong to sc=
rape the plain ends of molded fittings it is just that if not necessary one=
 can avoid increasing the gap between the socket and the plain end (for whi=
ch there is a limit and still allow a sound fusion).

J



--_000_4414AEBBCFB2B648B49E5766D309768E9804E34077MAIL_
